## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of cross-account access, data isolation, and automation in a multi-tenant SaaS architecture. It probes patterns beyond PrivateLink, focusing on RAM sharing and per-tenant bucket access controls.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles and trust policies
- AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) sharing
- S3 Access Points and bucket policies
- Organizations SCPs for guardrails
- Onboarding/offboarding automation and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Trust policy for cross-account role (AnalyticsAccount assumes TenantRole)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ANALYTICS_ACCOUNT_ID:root"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design enterprise-grade multi-tenant security architectures using AWS KMS, addressing real-world requirements for data sovereignty, tenant isolation, and key management in SaaS environments.

## Key Concepts
- Customer Managed Keys (CMKs) and tenant control
- Cross-account KMS access patterns
- Envelope encryption architecture
- Key rotation and revocation mechanisms
- Audit trails and compliance verification
- Incident response for key compromise

## Code Example
```json
